{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[supply]] with [[armour]] or (later especially) [[weapon]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The king '''armed''' his knights with swords and shields.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2015
|author=George R. R. Martin
|title=A Dance with Dragons
|publisher=Bantam
|isbn=9781101886038
|page=593
|passage=They were '''arming''' them with spears and shields, putting iron halfhelms on their heads, and arraying them along the inner wall, a rank of snowy sentinels. "Lord Winter has joined us with his levies," one of the sentries [said].}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figurative}} To supply with the [[equipment]], [[knowledge]], [[authority]]{{,}} or other [[tool]]s needed for a particular task; to [[furnish]] with [[capability]]; to [[equip]].
#* {{RQ:Jack Straw|I|14|thou getteſt no more of me.<br>For I am ſure thy Office doth not '''arme''' thee with ſuch authoritie.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|1 Peter|4|1|passage='''arm''' yourselves likewise with the same mind: for he that hath suffered in the flesh hath ceased from sin;}}
#* '''1801'''(?), John Bunyan, ''The Pilgrim's Progress ... to which is Added, the Life and Death of the Author'', page 359:
#*: Many following him, and, in his journeyings, he visited many at their houses, and gave them consolation, '''arming''' them with steady resolves, to be patient in suffering  and trust to God for their reward; {{...}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1806
|author=William turner
|title=An Abstract of the History of the Bible ... With questions for examination, etc
|page=43
|passage=[God] directed them to choose out three hundred only, and, '''arming''' them with nothing but trumpets and lamps, to send them by night into the camp of the Midianites.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1885|title=United States Congressional Serial Set|page=119
|passage=Q. In other words, you were commissioning men here in Cincinnati to attend the polls, '''arming''' them with authority to arrest citizens; men from outside of the city of Cincinnati to arrest citizens of the city of Cincinnati {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Meredith H. Lair|title=Armed with Abundance: Consumerism & Soldiering in the Vietnam War|publisher=Univ of North Carolina Press
|isbn=9780807834817
|page=215
|passage=Picture taking soothed support troops&#39; anxieties twice over, empowering them as they navigated a strange environment, and '''arming''' them with proof that they really had served in a war.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Susan Fawcett|title=Grassroots with Readings: The Writer's Workbook|publisher=Cengage Learning|isbn=9781305162853|page=466
|passage={{...}} and '''arming''' them with skills, work habits, and inner confidence that no one can ever take away.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[prepare]] (a [[tool]], [[weapon]], or [[system]]) for [[action]]; to [[activate]].
#: {{ux|en|Remember to '''arm''' the alarm system before leaving for work.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|of a [[tool]], [[weapon]], or [[system]]}} To become [[prepared]] for [[action]]; to [[activate]].
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Drachinifel|title=Guadalcanal Campaign - The Big Night Battle: Night 1 (IJN 3(?) : 2 USN)|date=10 March 2021|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Em_PuLURII4|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221017005233/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Em_PuLURII4|archivedate=17 October 2022|accessdate=6 November 2022|time=14:43|text=Torpedoes were loosed, but the range was too short for them to actually '''arm''', and they bounced harmlessly off the ship as it cut loose with its secondary and antiaircraft guns, smashing anything that it could see.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cover]] or [[furnish]] with a [[plate]], or with whatever will [[add]] [[strength]], [[force]], [[security]], or [[efficiency]].
#: {{co|en|to '''arm''' the hilt of a sword; to '''arm''' a hook in angling}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[take up]] [[weapon]]s; to arm oneself.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2 Feb 74|volume=1|number=32|journal=Gay Community News|page=14|author=Igor S. V. de Goldilox-Goldilox|title=Personal advertisement|text=Are you '''arming''', comrade Atheists?<br>Are you '''arming''' for the fray?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[fit]] (a [[magnet]]) with an [[armature]].

