==Scottish Gaelic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|gd|sga|arm||g=n|armour, battle-equipment, panoply; weapon; army}}, from {{der|gd|la|arma}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gd|/ˈaɾam/}}

===Noun===
{{gd-noun|g=m|gen=airm|pl=airm}}

# [[army]]
#: {{syn|gd|armailt}}
# {{l|en|arm}}, [[weapon]]

====Usage notes====
* '''Arm''' is usually used to refer to the entire fighting force of a nation etc, while '''armailt''' usually refers to the an "army" involved in a particular battle etc:
*: {{ux|gd|'''Arm''' Bhreatainn anns a' Chogadh Mhòr|inline=1|British Army in the First World War {{q|the armed forces as a whole}}}}
*: {{ux|gd|'''armailt''' Bhreatannach ann an Afraga|inline=1|British Army in Africa}}

